        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://townoflovell.com/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town proudly calls itself “The Rose Town of Wyoming” thanks to its historic ranching roots and blooming charm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townoflovell.com/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The EJZ Bridge over the Shoshone River, built in 1925, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lovell%2C_Wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lovell hosts the HyArt Historic Movie Theater, a landmark that showcases classic films and local history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
